erformed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171348409","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783#issuecomment-171348409","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783","id":171348409,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTM0ODQwOQ==","user":{"login":"ulfjack","id":7355745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTU3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack","html_url":"https://github.com/ulfjack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-13T16:22:00Z","updated_at":"2016-01-13T16:22:00Z","body":"That proposed refactoring seems like a rather big change - plug holes first, refactor later?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171348409/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ulfjack","id":7355745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTU3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack","html_url":"https://github.com/ulfjack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171570888","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783#issuecomment-171570888","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783","id":171570888,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTU3MDg4OA==","user":{"login":"lberki","id":3524818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjQ4MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3524818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki","html_url":"https://github.com/lberki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-14T08:29:22Z","updated_at":"2016-01-14T08:29:22Z","body":"Actually, it's just a few trivial lines of code, plugging the holes is more work.\n\nThe issue is that if you do the conversion when parsing the build file, `bazel query` will always return labels with a specified repository (i.e. `@//a/b:c/d`), which would wreak a lot of havoc internally. and it also won't be able to tell the difference between a label that got resolved to a particular repository because it was included in the original label or because the label didn't specify one and but was in that repository.\n\nMaybe a better idea is to tweak `bazel query` to return labels in the default repository if they refer to the repository they are in?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171570888/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"lberki","id":3524818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjQ4MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3524818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki","html_url":"https://github.com/lberki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171585809","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783#issuecomment-171585809","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783","id":171585809,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTU4NTgwOQ==","user":{"login":"ulfjack","id":7355745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTU3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack","html_url":"https://github.com/ulfjack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-14T09:35:17Z","updated_at":"2016-01-14T09:35:17Z","body":"There are two kinds of labels, absolute labels and relative labels. At this point in time, only @repository//foo:bar is an absolute label, everything else are relative labels (e.g., //foo:bar, :bar). Query should never output relative labels, except making that change would break a lot of preexisting software.\n\nI'd suggest to add a flag to query that makes it output the new absolute labels, and enabling that by default in Bazel. Internally, we'd disable that flag for now, check that all labels are in the main repository, and then only output //foo:bar.\n\nAlternatively, we could make query output relative labels for the main repository, but absolute ones for any other repository. Since we only have one repository internally, that would continue to work, while external users would get a mixture of absolute and relative labels as output. If we go with this approach, I'd still add a flag to query to make it always output absolute labels.\n\nThe only question I have is, what's the right absolute label for the main repository? Does the main repository have a name, or does it always use the empty string? @main//foo:bar or @//foo:bar?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171585809/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ulfjack","id":7355745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczNTU3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7355745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack","html_url":"https://github.com/ulfjack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ulfjack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/171595916","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783#issuecomment-171595916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/783","id":171595916,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3MTU5NTkxNg==","user":{"login":"lberki","id":3524818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjQ4MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3524818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki","html_url":"https://github.co